Wolfenstein 3D / Spear of Destiny for the Apple IIgs

Original game source and assets: id Software, https://github.com/id-Software/wolf3d.
The original limited-use license is retained in LICENSE-id.txt. Original game
music is by Bobby Prince. Apogee and FormGen published the original games.
This notice does not grant a new license for the game data.

Platform code and color-conversion tools include adaptations from IIgs Doom,
https://github.com/Webifi/iigs-doom. These cover boot/loading, disk packing,
B1 compression, DOC audio, input and build-host color conversion. The compiled
DOC player and other adapted platform code retain their source licenses;
this notice does not relicense them. The renderer and game logic follow
Wolfenstein 3D. No Doom game data is included.

ELF decoding and MAME test observers include adapted profiling infrastructure.
The build uses the original Wolf source tables and VGA palette data retained
under data/reference. Campaign picture and sound IDs follow the original DOS
headers. Original game graphics remain the property of their rights holders.

Menu item fonts: Black Ops One, with Alfa Slab One, Anton and Russo One retained
for the lettering tool. These fonts use SIL Open Font License 1.1. Complete
licenses and source hashes accompany the TTFs in tools/frontend/lettering/fonts.
The derived bitmap masks use other names. Original title pictures come from
Wolfenstein 3D; additional letter masks use those silhouettes as references.
The Cathedral attribution is a shape reference, not a verified production
credit. See tools/frontend/lettering/NOTICE.

The Wolf boot picture includes adapted mail-order cover art by Ken Rieger
(id Software, distributed by Apogee) and supplied loading artwork. Cover source:
https://fontsinuse.com/uses/53003/wolfenstein-3d-dos.

AdLib effect captures were made with Nuked-OPL3 in OPL2 mode, revision
765ec962e473aeb767e4cba74ffdc8f588ffbfe8:
https://github.com/nukeykt/Nuked-OPL3.
Nuked-OPL3 is copyright Nuke.YKT and LGPL-2.1-or-later. It is a build-time
renderer and is not linked into the IIgs program. Original effect data remains
id Software's game data.

Build-host TOML parsing: tools/vendor/tomli contains Tomli 2.2.1 by Taneli
Hukkinen, https://github.com/hukkin/tomli/tree/2.2.1, under its included MIT
license (tools/vendor/tomli/LICENSE). Python 3.11+ uses stdlib tomllib; the
bundled fallback supports Python 3.9/3.10.

Offline DOC previews: tools/doc_render.py and tools/doc_output.py follow the
MAME ES5503 behavior and Apple IIgs board-filter equations. The referenced
ES5503 implementation credits R. Belmont under BSD-3-Clause; see
tools/doc_model_LICENSE.txt. No MAME executable or Apple ROM is included or
needed for this path.
